{"explanation":"Update the existing AndroidKeyStore interoperability test to initialize AES/GCM encryption with an explicit fresh 96-bit nonce and 128-bit tag specification, authenticate the AES algorithm as AAD, and decrypt using the Cipher-produced AlgorithmParameters. This exercises the provider behavior that the coordinated EncryptedKey implementation relies on while preserving the test's existing assertion that an encrypt-only AndroidKeyStore key cannot decrypt. Per the prior semantic-validation requirement, this unrelated KeyStore access test does not directly invoke EncryptedKey; EncryptedKey-specific regression coverage remains in the coordinated EncryptedKeyTest file.","review_assumptions":["Supported AndroidKeyStore providers accept an explicitly supplied random 96-bit GCM nonce for AES/GCM/NoPadding encryption with an encrypt-only key.","Supported Android providers expose decryptable AlgorithmParameters after AES/GCM encryption initialized with GCMParameterSpec.","The coordinated EncryptedKeyTest supplies the direct EncryptedKey API regression coverage required by the cross-file plan; this test is limited to AndroidKeyStore/provider interoperability to satisfy prior validation feedback."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/KeyStoreAccessTest.java","original_code":"import java.io.IOException;
